        <item>
            <title>2.23.0</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 17:47:01 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>101</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.23.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features

- **Idle sessions now keep their conversation cached.** Every 55 minutes, each open pane whose session has gone quiet sends a short message and gets a one-word reply, so its prompt cache stays warm instead of lapsing. Rebuilding a lapsed cache costs roughly 20x what keeping one warm does, so coming back to a session you left overnight is cheaper with this on — by a margin measured in days, not hours.

  The refresh turns are hidden from the transcript, both while the session is open and when you reopen it later, and they do not light up the sidebar or the MacroPad. They do stay in that conversation's own history, which is what makes the cache hit work at all.

  Closing a pane stops refreshing it, and quitting stops all of them. There is a toggle in Settings if you would rather it were off.

### Changes

- Canopy declines to refresh a session that is busy, that is waiting on a permission prompt or a question, that runs against a custom API endpoint, or whose 5-hour usage window is above 80% — and it picks that last one back up once the window resets.
]]></description>
