        <item>
            <title>2.22.0</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 11:18:20 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>100</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.22.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features

- **Claude Fable is now selectable** from the launcher's Model menu.

### Changes

- The Model menu now lists model **families** instead of pinned versions — Fable, Opus, Opus (1M), Sonnet, Haiku. Each row follows the latest model in its family, so a newly released model shows up without waiting for a Canopy update.
- Removed the Opus 4.7 and Opus 4.8 entries, and the redundant Sonnet (1M) entry — Sonnet already runs with a 1M context window, so the two Sonnet rows were the same thing. Opus and Opus (1M) remain a real pair (200K and 1M).
- Existing selections are migrated automatically, so nothing has to be re-picked: Fable 5 → Fable, Opus 4.7 / Opus 4.8 → Opus, Opus 4.7 (1M) → Opus (1M), Sonnet (1M) → Sonnet.

### Known limitation

- With a custom model provider, the Fable row has no mapping to fall back on and will not resolve. This is unchanged from 2.21.0, which already listed a Fable entry.
]]></description>
